\title{Volcano and Manhattan Layer Processor}
\description{
Reads a \code{\link[=maidr_volcano]{maidr_volcano()}} or \code{\link[=maidr_manhattan]{maidr_manhattan()}} layer as the \code{volcano} or
\code{manhattan} trace. Both are scatters, so the point processor does the
work: the drawn rows, the positions read back through the scales, the
selector for the panel's points. What this adds is what the trace reads
that a scatter does not.
\itemize{
\item \strong{Each point's identity.} The geom's \code{label} and \code{region} aesthetics
survive the build as columns, and are emitted as the point's \code{label}
and \code{group} (the grammar's name for the region a point belongs to).
\item \strong{The threshold.} The layer's declared \code{thresholdOptions}, which the
core reads beside \code{data}, in the units the points are announced in.
}
}
